# Conventions Coding SoT

[`.specs/codebase/CONVENTIONS.md`](../../.specs/codebase/CONVENTIONS.md) is the **coding-conventions SoT**: naming, ESM/import style, dual-tsconfig, lint/format scripts.

It is **not** a changelog, stack/publish inventory, or UX cookbook.

**Ownership:** [DOC-OWNERSHIP.md](../../.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md).

## Forbidden in CONVENTIONS.md

- Milestone tags: `\bM\d+\b`
- Changelog / provenance voice (“shipped in M…”, “STATE decision”)
- Package publish facts (→ STACK); UX encyclopedias (→ cli-reference)

## Allowed

- `HOTSPOT-*` as a **naming convention** prefix pattern; `ADR-*`
- Present-tense coding conventions; pointers to ARCHITECTURE / AGENTS / CONTRIBUTING / STACK / commit-policy

## Sync rule

1. Update only when coding conventions change — do not append feature provenance.
2. Self-check: *Does this sentence need a milestone number to make sense?* If yes → ROADMAP/STATE/feature specs.

Editorial lint: [living-sot-doc.mjs](../hooks/lib/living-sot-doc.mjs) `lintConventionsDoc`.
